lar-nums\",\"children\":\"536\"}],[\"$\",\"td\",null,{\"className\":\"py-2 tabular-nums font-medium\",\"children\":\"21.3\"}],[\"$\",\"td\",null,{\"className\":\"py-2 tabular-nums text-right text-ink-muted\",\"children\":\"16w\"}]]}]]}]]}]]}],\"$L1b\"]}]]}]\n18:[\"$\",\"section\",null,{\"className\":\"rounded-2xl border border-line bg-surface p-6\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"h2\",null,{\"className\":\"text-base font-semibold text-ink mb-4\",\"children\":\"Builder notes\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"text-sm text-ink leading-relaxed whitespace-pre-line\",\"children\":\"This is the Lianda T44 designed for thin mini-ITX motherboards with strict 25mm IO shield height requirement. CPU cooler limited to 27mm maximum. The case has minimal cooling with no top cutouts and poor side airflow; the builder cut a large hole in the top panel and installed a nylon mesh cover, which improved temperatures by ~10C and doubled CPU performance. The 35w TDP i5-12400T was power-limited to 29w. The integrated graphics (Intel UHD 730) is extremely weak, suitable only for office work and light video viewing, not gaming. Performance is very basic but runs faster than Raspberry Pi 4/5. Case requires modification for adequate cooling and is only recommended for basic desktop use, home server applications, or industrial low-power headless servers. Would NOT recommend without the top mesh modification.\"}]]}]\n19:[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"space-y-4\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"section\",null,{\"className\":\"rounded-2xl border border-line bg-surface p-5 space-y-4\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"h2\",null,{\"className\":\"text-base font-semibold text-ink\",\"children\":\"Performance\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"text-xs text-ink-muted uppercase tracking-wide font-medium mb-1\",\"children\":\"CPU — CB23 Multi\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"text-2xl font-bold text-ink tabular-nums\",\"children\":\"6,306\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"